A||||3||Ozzy||This site is AWSOME!!  Cudo's and appreciation!
Z||000000||Ozzy||08-08-99||03:02 AM||||Hey folks...<p>I have owned a Fiero '88 coupe, 2.5l, 5 speed, for about one month. It's my first Fiero and with that comes foriegn teritory. I have owned several different vehicles since coming to the U.S. (I'm Australian and have lived here 9 yrs) of various years makes and models and have refused to work on any of them due to computers and weird looking stuff foriegn to me from my old wrenching days on Australian cars. (Swapped and engine in a '84 Bronco II once...piece of junk!)<p>Enter the Internet. A usefull information rescource for everything, but none as much as for this particular activity. I have been scouring the net for Fiero related material and have found lots of info and advertising for after market stuff as well as some usefull FAQ and other forum pages but this forum kicks 'em all into the weeds!! There is something of a lead at least, if not the direct problem itself being answered by knowledgable folks who have taken the time to share their findings with others. Considering how easy it is to get royaly reemed by the automotive trades I think this is a very valuable rescource. <p>To the creators and contributors I extend my gratitude as I'm sure many, many others who come here will also.<p>Ozzy the 'Aussie'
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||08-08-99||02:12 PM||||Hi Ozzy, and welcome! Good to see someone from "down under" visiting!
Z||000002||PaUL||08-09-99||06:25 PM||||I was just thinking about how the internet has revolutionized the marketing and sale of all kinds of products. I bought my fiero 10 years ago and immediately did an engine swap from the 2.5 to 2.8 v6. I got all my parts from the local GM dealer. It makes me sick to see that I can now get the same parts for less than half of what I paid a decade ago. For example, it cost me close to $200 to replace a headlight motor from the dealer, now I see them selling for $85 on an online parts site. I even found a site that sells used ones in good condition for $35. I buy almost everything over net now. If a retailer doesnt have a web site with online catalog and ordering, I dont buy from them.
Z||000003||DJRice||08-10-99||07:02 AM||||I like that we are no longer 'at the mercy' or a mechanic or dealership.  When one of us has a problem, all we have to do is post it.  Most of the time someone else has had the problem and solved it.  This forum definitely makes it easier to be a 'shadetree mechanic'.<p>Dillon<br>
